.TH HELIKODU-SCAN-WORKER 1 2026-11-18 Helikodu "User Commands"
.SH NAME
helikodu\-scan\-worker \- read the tags and properties of audio files for the Helikodu library scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B helikodu\-scan\-worker
.RB [ \-\-memory\-limit
.IR bytes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B helikodu\-scan\-worker
is a helper program of Helikodu; it is not meant to be started by hand.
.BR helikodu (1)
and
.BR helikodu\-cli (1)
start one or more of these processes when they scan the library, measure
loudness or read files again after their tags were written, and send them
one file at a time over the standard input and output.
The protocol between them is internal and may change between versions.
.PP
Reading a damaged or hostile file can crash or hang a decoder library.
Doing the reading in a separate process with limited resources means that
such a file stops only the worker, which is then started again, never the
application.
Before it reads anything, the worker limits its own address space and turns
core dumps off; the limits cannot be raised again from inside the process.
Tracker modules, game music, SID tunes and MIDI files are read by their own
decoders, which also report the songs a file holds; every other file is read
through FFmpeg.
.PP
The programs look for the worker beside themselves and in
.I ../libexec/helikodu/
relative to their own folder;
.B helikodu\-cli
also takes another path with
.BR \-\-worker .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-memory\-limit " bytes"
The address-space limit of the process in bytes.
The default is 1 GiB; 0 sets no limit.
Also accepted as
.BI \-\-memory\-limit= bytes\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The input was closed after the last request.
.TP
.B 1
The limits could not be set, or reading or writing a request failed.
.TP
.B 2
An unknown argument or a limit that is not a number.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <prefix>/libexec/helikodu/helikodu\-scan\-worker
Where an installation puts the program.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR helikodu (1),
.BR helikodu\-cli (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/sorrelfox/helikodu/issues
.UE .
